ref 17592186045417] [17592186575508 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575508 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575508 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186574972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575508 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d53eb4df-306d-5fe9-a04a-ef268bb57a12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575560 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186575508 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575560 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129487" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575560 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575560 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the equation of the tangent hyperplane to the hypersurface $w={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}$ at the point $(1,0,2,5).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575560 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6f62591f-ce02-5d1d-a041-40b4fa4f0093" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575560 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the hypersurface $w=f(x,y,z)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0},{w}_{0})$ on the hypersurface can be written as\n\n$$\nw-{w}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})+(z-{z}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂z}({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})=2x \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})=-2y \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z} & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})=2z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y,z)=(1,0,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,0,2) & =2(1)=2 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,0,2) & =-2(0)=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,0,2) & =2(2)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent hyperplane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}w-5 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,0,2)+(y-0)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,0,2)+(z-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂z}(1,0,2) \\\\ w-5 & =2(x-1)+0y+4(z-2) \\\\ w-5 & =2x+4z-10 \\\\ 2x+4z-w-5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575622 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186575453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575622 #edb/ref 1069 "q-129445" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575622 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575622 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z={x}^{3}{y}^{2}-2$ at the point $(1,2,2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575622 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f74663e2-eda6-5c43-8b1e-ec79f6eff3d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186575622 #edb/ref 1074 "The Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the surface $z=f(x,y)$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ on the surface can be written as\n\n$$\nz-{z}_{0}=(x-{x}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂x}({x}_{0},{y}_{0})+(y-{y}_{0})\\frac{∂f}{∂y}({x}_{0},{y}_{0}).\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}{y}^{2}-2) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}{y}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}{y}^{2}-2) \\\\  & =2{x}^{3}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the partial derivatives at $(x,y)=(1,2):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,2) & =3({1}^{2})({2}^{2})=12 \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,2) & =2({1}^{3})(2)=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write down the equation of the tangent plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-2 & =(x-1)\\frac{∂f}{∂x}(1,2)+(y-2)\\frac{∂f}{∂y}(1,2) \\\\ z-2 & =12(x-1)+4(y-2) \\\\ z-2 & =12x+4y-20 \\\\ 12x+4y-z-18 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
